    "case_summary": "A 72-year-old female with a BMI of 19.23 presented with intermittent pain in right lumbar and abdomen with chills and fever for 1 year. The symptoms would relieve with anti-inflammatory therapy but recurred repeatedly. Patient was previously physically fit, with no history of coronary disease, hypertension, diabetes, or chronic bronchitis.\n\nPhysical examination showed no obvious positive signs.\n\n- Imaging Studies:    1. CT Examination:       Image Title: Preoperative ureteral imaging       Image Description: Shows proximal ureter dilation and hydronephrosis           2. Additional CT Findings:       Image Title: Preoperative CT       Image Description: Revealed herniation into the greater sciatic foramen with proximal ureteral dilatation",
